{
  "profile": "provenance-anchor.v0",
  "description": "provenance-anchor.v0 \u2014 build-first ORIGINATION gate. A record declares its `claim`: `origination` (the anchor tx MUST commit the sha256 digest of a canonical anchor-binding.v0 object naming proposal{kind,id,repo}+artifact{repo,commit}) or `pre_existence` (only witnessed precedence). A PASS carries its claim \u2014 PASS:origination | PASS:pre_existence \u2014 so pre-existence can never read as origination (@zexoverz/Faisal). Facts: content identity; existence witness (independent, never self-reported); anchor subject binding; thread subject binding (forge_event in the proposal's CANONICAL repo that ADDs the exact-case ERCS/erc-<id>.md); anchor->proposal binding (origination only: resolver recomputes the binding digest and checks the tx calldata commits it; optional signer->originator); witnessed precedence. `resolution` is a MODEL INPUT. REAL & DEMOTED: the on-chain 8299 (0xc3aeb16d\u2026, calldata commits sha256('hello')) and 8373 (0x04e1846f\u2026) anchors carry NO proposal binding, so they are pre_existence only, not origination. `ctrl-8299-tx-in-8373-not-bound` is Faisal's exact attack \u2014 a free-standing pre-existing tx placed in an origination record \u2014 and it FAILs anchor_not_bound. `origination-model-pass`/`-signer-pass` are MODEL fixtures pending a real minted anchor. Synthetic ordering controls use proposal id>=90000 / PR>=990000. Counts: 5 PASS / 17 FAIL / 13 UNVERIFIABLE = 35. Origination is a committed binding, never a coincidence of timing.",
